{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"Q6QRN9","secondaryAccessions":["A0A5G2RDZ2"],"uniProtkbId":"ADT3_PIG","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"2004-09-13","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-09-02","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"2026-01-28","entryVersion":123,"sequenceVersion":4},"annotationScore":4.0,"organism":{"scientificName":"Sus scrofa","commonName":"Pig","taxonId":9823,"lineage":["Eukaryota","Metazoa","Chordata","Craniata","Vertebrata","Euteleostomi","Mammalia","Eutheria","Laurasiatheria","Artiodactyla","Suina","Suidae","Sus"]},"proteinExistence":"2: Evidence at transcript level","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"ADP/ATP translocase 3"}},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P12236"}],"value":"ADP,ATP carrier protein 3"}},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P12236"}],"value":"Adenine nucleotide translocator 3"},"shortNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P12236"}],"value":"ANT 3"}]},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Solute carrier family 25 member 6"}}],"contains":[{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"ADP/ATP translocase 3, N-terminally processed"}}}]},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P12236"}],"value":"SLC25A6"},"synonyms":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P12236"}],"value":"AAC3"},{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P12236"}],"value":"ANT3"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"G2QNH0"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P12236"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P48962"}],"value":"ADP:ATP antiporter that mediates import of ADP into the mitochondrial matrix for ATP synthesis, and export of ATP out to fuel the cell (By similarity). Cycles between the cytoplasmic-open state (c-state) and the matrix-open state (m-state): operates by the alternating access mechanism with a single substrate-binding site intermittently exposed to either the cytosolic (c-state) or matrix (m-state) side of the inner mitochondrial membrane (By similarity). In addition to its ADP:ATP antiporter activity, also involved in mitochondrial uncoupling and mitochondrial permeability transition pore (mPTP) activity (By similarity). Plays a role in mitochondrial uncoupling by acting as a proton transporter: proton transport uncouples the proton flows via the electron transport chain and ATP synthase to reduce the efficiency of ATP production and cause mitochondrial thermogenesis. Proton transporter activity is inhibited by ADP:ATP antiporter activity, suggesting that SLC25A6/ANT3 acts as a master regulator of mitochondrial energy output by maintaining a delicate balance between ATP production (ADP:ATP antiporter activity) and thermogenesis (proton transporter activity). Proton transporter activity requires free fatty acids as cofactor, but does not transport it (By similarity). Also plays a key role in mPTP opening, a non-specific pore that enables free passage of the mitochondrial membranes to solutes of up to 1.5 kDa, and which contributes to cell death (By similarity). It is however unclear if SLC25A6/ANT3 constitutes a pore-forming component of mPTP or regulates it (By similarity)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"ADP(in) + ATP(out) = ADP(out) + ATP(in)","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:34999"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:30616"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:456216"}],"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P48962"}]}},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"H(+)(in) = H(+)(out)","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:34979"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15378"}],"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P48962"}]}},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"G2QNH0"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P48962"}],"value":"The matrix-open state (m-state) is inhibited by the membrane-permeable bongkrekic acid (BKA). The cytoplasmic-open state (c-state) is inhibited by the membrane-impermeable toxic inhibitor carboxyatractyloside (CATR) (By similarity). Proton transporter activity is inhibited by ADP:ATP antiporter activity (By similarity)"}],"commentType":"ACTIVITY REGULATION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"G2QNH0"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P02722"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P32007"}],"value":"Monomer (By similarity). Found in a complex with ARL2, ARL2BP and SLC25A6/ANT3 (By similarity)"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","note":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P12235"}],"value":"The complex formed with ARL2BP, ARL2 and SLC25A6/ANT3 is expressed in mitochondria (By similarity). May localize to non-mitochondrial membranes (By similarity)"}]},"subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P02722"}],"value":"Mitochondrion inner membrane","id":"SL-0168"},"topology":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255"}],"value":"Multi-pass membrane protein","id":"SL-9909"}},{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P12236"}],"value":"Membrane","id":"SL-0162"},"topology":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255"}],"value":"Multi-pass membrane protein","id":"SL-9909"}}]},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P02722"}],"value":"The transmembrane helices are not perpendicular to the plane of the membrane, but cross the membrane at an angle. Odd-numbered transmembrane helices exhibit a sharp kink, due to the presence of a conserved proline residue"}],"commentType":"DOMAIN"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P12236"}],"value":"Trimethylated by ANTKMT at Lys-52"}],"commentType":"PTM"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Belongs to the mitochondrial carrier (TC 2.A.29) family"}],"commentType":"SIMILARITY"}],"features":[{"type":"Chain","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":298,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"ADP/ATP translocase 3","featureId":"PRO_0000425782"},{"type":"Initiator methionine","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Removed; alternate","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P12236"}]},{"type":"Chain","location":{"start":{"value":2,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":298,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"ADP/ATP translocase 3, N-terminally processed","featureId":"PRO_0000090585"},{"type":"Topological domain","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":7,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Mitochondrial intermembrane","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}]},{"type":"Transmembrane","location":{"start":{"value":8,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":37,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Helical; Name=1","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P02722"}]},{"type":"Topological domain","location":{"start":{"value":38,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":74,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Mitochondrial matrix","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}]},{"type":"Transmembrane","location":{"start":{"value":75,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":99,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Helical; Name=2","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB",